     "*   **Block Definition:** $B_\\nu = [i_0, i_1] \\times [j_0, j_1] \\times [k_0, k_1]$.",
     "For a cell, compute the value range (convex hull) for its four left voxels and set a ternary flag (-1 if $t$ below, 0 if in, 1 if above).",
     "Cell is active if both flags are zero or have opposite sign.",
     "The right flag of one cell is the left flag of the next, avoiding recomputation.",
     "*   **Interval Tree ($a=2$):** Uses min/max lists and interval tree structure.",
     "*   **Kd-Tree ($a=3$):** Uses pointerless kd-tree on span space.",
     "*   **Out-of-Core ($a=4$):** Uses external interval tree.",
     "Memory on disk: High (e.g., 1261 MB for X MAS dataset).",
     "Enumeration is $O(|B|)$, Interval/Kd-trees are output-sensitive or logarithmic.",
     "The method optimally utilizes available memory, unlike fixed methods.",
     "*   **Kd-Tree:** 1087 ms, 837 MB. 1530x speedup.",
     "*   **Interval Tree:** 17.14 ms, 1256 MB. 3000x speedup.",
     "*   **Out-of-Core:** 2500 ms, 0 MB main memory (1261 MB external).",
     "Significantly faster than out-of-core-only or octree-only methods when memory is partially available.",
     "Kd-tree estimation has <5% error but requires downsampling.",
     "Lagrangian optimization only finds points on the lower convex hull, causing gaps in the memory-time curve."
    ]
